<title>UK: World Bank adds 500 mln Czech crown to one-yr bond.</title>
<headline>World Bank adds 500 mln Czech crown to one-yr bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond has been</p>
<p>increased to 2.0 billion Czech crowns from 1.5 billion Czech</p>
<p>crowns, lead manager HSBC Markets said.</p>
<p> BORROWER   WORLD BANK</p>
<p> AMT   *2.0 BLN CZK   COUPON     10.50     MATURITY    06.MAY.98</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.95    PAY DATE  **23.MAY.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.0	 REOFFER    100.10 PLUS 17 DAYS ACCRUED INTEREST</p>
<p> MOODY	=	   LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  =	   DENOMS (K) 25	  SALE LIMITS US/UK/CZ</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    15 BP     SELL CONC  85 BP     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES	*ORIGINALLY LAUNCHED FOR 1.5 BILLION CZK ON 18.APR.97</p>
<p>		 UNSECURED</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
